# GuardianAI - Engineering Onboarding Document

Welcome to GuardianAI (also referred to internally as CivicProof). This document is your complete engineering handover guide. It is designed to take you from a high-level understanding of the product all the way down to the low-level implementation details of the codebase. Read this document thoroughly before making your first code change.

---

## 1. Executive Summary

**GuardianAI** is a modern civic-tech web application designed to streamline the reporting and resolution of community infrastructure hazards (such as potholes, broken streetlights, or illegal dumping). 

Historically, municipal issues go unreported due to friction in reporting systems, or they take too long to fix with little transparency. Furthermore, cities often struggle with fraudulent reports or workers claiming to have fixed an issue without actually visiting the site. 

GuardianAI solves these business problems by providing a unified platform where:
- **Citizens** can report issues simply by snapping a photo.
- **Workers** (field staff) are dispatched to resolve issues and must provide photographic proof of resolution.
- **Authorities** monitor a real-time dashboard of all civic issues.

The core innovation of GuardianAI is its **AI-driven validation pipeline**. When a citizen uploads a photo, a custom ML model automatically classifies the hazard. When a worker submits a resolution photo, the system verifies their live GPS coordinates against the original report and uses computer vision to visually match the "before" and "after" photos, ensuring the issue was legitimately resolved.

The project is currently at a prototype/MVP maturity level. It features a React-based Single Page Application (SPA), a Node.js/Express core API, and a decoupled Python Flask microservice handling the heavy AI workloads.

