## 20. Common Pitfalls

- **ML Service Port Binding:** The ML service runs on port `5000`. If you have an instance of Control Center or another service running on port 5000, Flask will crash on startup.
- **Base64 Payload Size:** If users upload 4K images from modern smartphones, the base64 string can exceed Express's default limits. We've set it to `"10mb"`, but very large images might still trigger `413 Payload Too Large`.
- **Missing Auth Middleware:** Do not assume API routes are protected. The controllers currently lack backend JWT validation checks.

